r mental health services for perpetrator of nonparental child neglect","id":52,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[72.0,548.09,510.5,560.25],"firstLineX":72.0,"indent":0,"small":false},{"id":"b15","kind":"marker","spans":[{"t":"825","id":53,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[297.0,577.05,315.0,589.05],"firstLineX":297.0,"indent":60,"small":false},{"id":"b16","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"t":"Child Psychological Abuse","id":54,"b":true,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"This category may be used when psychological abuse of a child is a focus of clinical attention.","id":55,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"Child psychological abuse is nonaccidental verbal or symbolic acts by a child’s parent or","id":56,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"caregiver that result, or have reasonable potential to result, in significant psychological harm to","id":57,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"the child. (Physical and sexual abusive acts are not included in this category.) Examples of","id":58,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"psychological abuse of a child include berating, disparaging, or humiliating the child; threatening","id":59,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"the child; harming/abandoning—or indicating that the alleged offender will harm/abandon—","id":60,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false},{"t":" "},{"t":"people or things that the child cares about; confining the child (as by tying a child’s arms or legs","id":61,"b":false,"i":false,"s":false}],"level":4,"bbox":[72.0,603.29,539.78,716.25],"firstLineX":72.0,"indent":0,"small":false}],"figures":[],"ocr":null,"nativeTextSha256":"0461b58c6ab4b2eec6b76ad6d41001d979f13ff83a90d02efebd466d62e31fcd","nativeCharacters":2361,"sparse":false,"tableCount":0}